{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1008155-enemy-type-breakdown-new-solar-charms-like-firearms","id":1008155,"title":"Enemy Type Breakdown + New Solar charms (like firearms)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T09:53:26-08:00","id":1008155,"title":"Enemy Type Breakdown + New Solar charms (like firearms)","content":"When making my monster manual I figured doing something like breaking down the monster types into three areas which ST's can use would be useful. Insignificant, Normal, and Special. Special characters are those with activate initiative tracks and can make decisive attacks, Normal are kinda like elite soldiers that share some things in common with battle groups, but unlike battle groups you can fit several under one roof. I'd format it for the boards, but I'm about to get going to my job right now so have the google document which you can comment on (I'll also be reading this)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-3Zbu9Ky0nWpvh4rwed_YKq3QAlaxzmzkHrIxegw3-E/edit#\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-3Zbu9Ky0nWpvh4rwed_YKq3QAlaxzmzkHrIxegw3-E/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-3Zbu9Ky0nWpvh4rwed_YKq3QAlaxzmzkHrIxegw3-E/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-3Zbu9Ky0nWpvh4rwed_YKq3QAlaxzmzkHrIxegw3-E/edit# </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Think of this as the Thanksgiving day present for the charms. I'll also note these homebrew rules are optional (no